<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises benchmark crude price for June.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises benchmark crude price for June.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) has raised by 15 cents the price of its benchmark Gulf of Suez blend against Dated Brent for June, an EGPC official told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>The official said EGPC had also raised prices by 10 to 15 cents of five other crudes. Following are details of June crude prices, all against Dated Brent (May differentials in brackets):</p>
<p>    Gulf of Suez	-$2.50 (-$2.65)</p>
<p>    Belayim	     -$3.65 (-$3.80)</p>
<p>    Ras Gharib	  -$4.25 (-$4.40)</p>
<p>    Ras Badran	  -$3.70 (-$3.85)</p>
<p>    Ras el-Behar	-$2.05 (-$2.15)</p>
<p>    Zeit Bay	    -$2.10 (-$2.20)</p>
<p>-- Esmat Salaheddin +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
